        "original_id": "aa17bea1-5f33-5f7a-b291-a91dfac71cf3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tiffany Darwish\n- Organizations: The Beatles, Billboard\n- Products: \"Could've Been,\" \"I Saw Him Standing There,\" \"I Saw Her Standing There,\" \"Please Please Me\"\n- Topics: music covers, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- The Beatles released \"I Saw Her Standing There\" as the opening track on their 1963 debut album \"Please Please Me.\"\n- Tiffany Renee Darwish, born October 2, 1971, is an American singer, songwriter, actress, and former teen icon.\n- Tiffany Darwish recorded \"I Saw Him Standing There\" as a cover version of The Beatles' \"I Saw Her Standing There.\"\n- An album discussed in this chunk includes a cover of The Beatles song \"I Saw Her Standing There.\"\n- Tiffany Darwish released the singles \"Could've Been\" and \"I Saw Him Standing There\" soon after, and \"Could've Been\" reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100.",
